uses on *verification* and *enforcement* of the logging requirements during the development cycle.\n    *   It prevents \"logging drift\" where new features are added but logs aren't updated, which is a common failure point in complex R&D environments.\n    *   By failing builds, it forces developers to treat compliance as a first-class requirement (like a unit test), significantly reducing the risk of audit failure.\n\n    *   Rationale: This proposal implements \"compliance-as-code,\" ensuring that Article 12 requirements are technically enforced throughout the development lifecycle and preventing costly retrofits or regulatory breaches at launch. It transforms a passive legal requirement into an active engineering constraint.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: High (95+). This is a gold-standard way to handle regulatory technical requirements in a software environment.",
