archers, allowing them to maintain iteration speed (\"keeping iteration speed flat\").\n\n    *   Does it serve my domain of concern? Yes, by protecting research velocity and enabling scientific traceability.\n    *   Is it a waste of resources from an R&D perspective? No, because manual implementation across every project is a massive drain on high-value researchers. An SDK approach is efficient.\n    *   Is there any downside to my specific vantage point? Minimal. It's not \"research\" in the sense of a paper, but it's \"research infrastructure.\"\n\n    *   *Rationale:* Automating the logging requirements removes repetitive engineering overhead from research teams and ensures a rigorous, standardized audit trail necessary for scientific reproducibility and compliance without slowing down exploration.\n    *   *Decision:* Approve.\n    *   *Promise Score:* High (around 85-90). It's an extremely practical tool that solves a systemic friction point between regulatory needs and research agility.",
