al audits.\n    *   Are there risks? The primary risk is a \"false positive\" in the audit script (saying it's compliant when it isn't), but even then, having a formal gate is better than no gate.\n\n    *   Rationale: This proposal directly mitigates the high legal and financial risk of non-compliance by enforcing Article 12(3) requirements as a hard technical constraint before deployment. It replaces unreliable manual oversight with an automated gate, protecting the institution's survival and reputation.\n    *   Decision: Approve.\n    *   Promise: High (95+). It is a classic \"compliance-by-design\" approach.",
