tacle to \"innovative AI.\"\n\n    *   The proposal is pragmatic. It leverages existing infrastructure (experiment tracking) to satisfy legal requirements.\n    *   From a research perspective, reducing friction between the \"lab\" and \"compliance\" is highly desirable.\n    *   It doesn't introduce new research constraints; it simply organizes data collection efficiently.\n\n    *   Rationale: Integrating regulatory logging into the existing experiment-tracking stack enhances end-to-end traceability from training to deployment without introducing fragmented infrastructure that would hinder researcher productivity. This approach supports scientific reproducibility by unifying development and operational telemetry.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: 85 (High, because it's efficient and maintains a clean R&D workflow, though the technical \"mapping\" success depends on the flexibility of the existing schema).",
